WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:10.593
Ahh.

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:11.594
Ahh.

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:14.264
Two more, coming right up.

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.766
Bucky's got all the luck.

00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:18.643
Yeah, she's pretty.

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:19.477
No, not that.

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:21.438
Lucky b*stard is shipping out tomorrow.

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:23.356
He's going to be a stone's throw away
from the Kr*uts

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.691
while the rest of us will still be flying practice

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.234
missions over Nebraska.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.738
Don't worry, we'll be over there
dropping bombs soon enough.

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:32.073
Bucky, next round's on us.

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:33.908
He's never done that before.

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:36.286
So you're Bucky, and he's Buck?

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:38.288
Eh, it's a long story.

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:39.873
They make a nice pair, don't they?

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.709
Ah, I should have introduced them earlier.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.294
He's leaving tomorrow.

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:46.212
Everyone needs someone
to write to back home.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.548
I don't know if John Egan's the pen pal type.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.430
Well, maybe if he met a girl worth writing to,
he would be.

00:00:56.139 --> 00:00:58.433
A girl worth writing to is hard to find.

00:00:58.433 --> 00:00:59.976
Not if you know where to look.

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:05.356
I see what you mean.

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:07.484
So you'll write me?

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:09.068
Well, I already have.

00:01:09.944 --> 00:01:11.488
You wrote me a letter?

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:12.655
Yeah.

00:01:12.655 --> 00:01:13.740
What's it say?

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.284
Well, you'll have to wait and find out.

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:18.286
Well, when will that be?

00:01:18.286 --> 00:01:19.245
Oh, when I ship out.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.914
I'd say two or three weeks.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.546
I'm going to miss you every second.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.298
All right, all right.

00:01:30.298 --> 00:01:31.549
Gentlemen, a toast.

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:34.969
Buck, Marge, hey, you lovebirds,
we're toasting Bucky over here.

00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:36.554
Hear, hear, Major Egan.

00:01:36.554 --> 00:01:38.973
To our new air exec, Bucky.

00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:39.682
All right, Major.

00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:41.267
Of all the drunks in the 100th.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.145
Well, someone's got to make a nest
for the rest of you dodos.

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:45.271
Cheers, Major.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:45.813
To the 100th.

00:01:45.813 --> 00:01:46.231
To the 100th.

00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:47.065
Best of luck, sir.

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.608
Good luck, sir.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.108
Thanks.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:50.193
Save some Kr*uts for us.

00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:51.236
We're going to Slooter's.

00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:52.028
You guys coming?

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:52.528
Nah.

00:01:52.528 --> 00:01:53.863
I got to fly early.

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:54.781
Buck?

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.407
I don't think so, boys.

00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:57.659
See you tomorrow then.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:01:58.326
Bye, Marge.

00:01:58.326 --> 00:01:59.869
Bucky, see you in England.

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:03.831
And remember, I want extra blankets
and a cot with a view.

00:02:03.831 --> 00:02:05.291
Consider it done.

00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:07.669
He won't tell me.

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:09.087
What's with the nicknames?

00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:10.088
Spill, Marge.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:10.588
Go ahead.

00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:11.089
Go ahead.

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:12.257
Told you, it's a long story.

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:17.011
Well, they met in basic training
before the war started.

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:21.099
John, uh– John was always Bucky
since he was a kid, right?

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.141
That's right, yeah.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:29.357
And Gale well,
Gale's always been Gale, until–

00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:32.402
First day of basic training,
this fella walks up to me

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:34.320
and says that I remind him of a guy back

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.447
home in, uh, Wisconsin.

00:02:36.447 --> 00:02:38.700
Goes by the name of Buck.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.577
I tell him my name's Gale, Gale Cleven.

00:02:41.577 --> 00:02:45.081
And Bucky here, he's not deterred.

00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:48.292
No, sir, it's just Buck this, Buck that.

00:02:48.292 --> 00:02:49.919
Buck, can you help me tie my shoes?

00:02:49.919 --> 00:02:52.171
Buck, help me fly this plane.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.382
Before I know it, the whole damn
Eighth Air Force

00:02:54.382 --> 00:02:55.591
is calling me Buck.

00:02:55.591 --> 00:02:57.427
What kind of a name is Gale anyway?

00:02:57.427 --> 00:02:58.094
Oh.

00:02:58.094 --> 00:03:00.179
You know what-- you know what,
you should actually

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:00.888
be thanking me.

00:03:00.888 --> 00:03:01.973
I did you a favor.

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:03.099
For giving me the same name as you?

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:04.142
It's not exactly the same name.

00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:05.893
And it's not my fault you look exactly

00:03:05.893 --> 00:03:08.271
like Buck from Manitowoc–

00:03:08.271 --> 00:03:08.896
From Manitowoc.

00:03:08.896 --> 00:03:09.480
–Wisconsin.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.566
What kind of man does that to
his best friend?

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:13.401
Oh, it's so sweet.

00:03:13.401 --> 00:03:14.694
We need music.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:15.862
OK, don't go away.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:20.241
Gale– Buck–
you're going to dance with me

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:21.659
before this night is through.

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:23.578
Oh, don't make me dance, Marge.

00:03:26.456 --> 00:03:29.751
Pick a good one,
Artie Shaw, Benny Goodman.

00:03:30.585 --> 00:03:34.881
Hey, you know,
I am amazed that we're friends.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.425
You don't like to dance
with a beautiful woman.

00:03:37.425 --> 00:03:38.301
You don't drink.

00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:39.802
You don't gamble.

00:03:39.802 --> 00:03:40.928
You don't even like sports.

00:03:40.928 --> 00:03:43.181
Well, we are one of life's great mysteries.

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:55.651
[JUKEBOX PLAYING]

00:03:55.651 --> 00:03:56.819
Oh, I love that.

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:57.445
Yes.

00:03:57.445 --> 00:03:57.945
Yeah?

00:04:00.948 --> 00:04:06.496
[EXHALING] So this is it?

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.123
This is it.

00:04:09.832 --> 00:04:11.209
See you in a few weeks.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.377
If I don't die first.

00:04:14.128 --> 00:04:15.963
Hate to break it to you, Bucky,
but you are

00:04:15.963 --> 00:04:18.299
the 100th's air executive now.

00:04:18.299 --> 00:04:20.593
You're not going over there
to fly missions.

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:23.679
Look, I, uh–
I had a conversation with the CO

00:04:23.679 --> 00:04:25.765
over at the 389th,
and I'm flying with those boys

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.266
until you guys show up.

00:04:27.892 --> 00:04:29.727
I'll be an observation pilot.

00:04:30.561 --> 00:04:32.813
You son of a b*tch.

00:04:32.813 --> 00:04:35.650
Yeah, well, someone's gotta
taste a little combat,

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.735
tell you what it's really like up there.

00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:41.739
Well, don't you die on me
before I get over there.

00:04:43.032 --> 00:04:44.075
Don't count on it.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.454
Keep your nose down.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.748
Let's get this fire out.

00:04:50.748 --> 00:04:52.250
Come on, faster.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.710
You have to help us.

